\\ PROFILE.SEQ          Profile a Forth word            by Tom Zimmer
\\                                                      F-PC native port

  This file provides the ability to profile a large F-PC application.
Words that consume large amounts of execution time are detected, and
accumulated into a 32k external array.

  The operation of this profiller is almost completely transparent to
the operation of your program.  A change is made to the DOS system clock,
to accumulate counts of where an application is each time a clock tick
occurs. PROFILE saves a count of each occurance of a particular "ES" (the
F-PC colon definition pointer) on each clock tick. After the application
terminates, PROFILE writes the accumulated results to a file called
PROF.TXT. The file will contain the paragraph of each word accumulated,
the count of how many times that paragraph was found, and the name of the
Forth word that starts at that paragraph.

  This profiler is different from most, in that doesn't try to measure
the performance of code words, it will in fact accumulate the time of any
code word executed, into the time of the colon definition that used it.
While this may seem odd, it is correct, as most of F-PC Forths CODE time
is spent in words like NEXT, NEST, and UNNEST which are as highly
optimized as they can be.  The primary use of PROFILE is to detect
algorithm problems in your program. Since counts are only performed at 18
times a second, you will need to profile a fairly long (in execution
time) program to get useful results.

  Native port: there is no timer interrupt and no 8086 NEXT to patch.
The VM's debugger trace hook (see DEBUG.SEQ: DBG-ON DBG-LO DBG-HI 'DEBUG)
is used instead: while profiling, every token executed in list space calls
PROF-TICK, a CODE word (abstract machine, so it runs JIT compiled) that
adds one to a count cell for that IP and re-arms the hook. So the counts
are exact numbers of tokens executed in each colon definition (and DOES>
clause), not clock ticks; the time spent inside a primitive or CODE word
still goes to the colon definition that called it, as before. A program
runs several times slower while it is profiled.

  Words compiled after PROF_START are not counted. PROF.TXT lists, in
dictionary order, each definition with a count of at least PROF-MIN: the
count, its percentage of the total, and the name (a DOES> clause counts
for the defining word it is in). .PROF shows the same report on the
screen. The DEBUG debugger and the profiler share the hook, so don't use
both at once.

  PROFILE can be used in two ways:

        PROF <word_name> <enter>

  will profile <word_name>, and write results to PROF.TXT. You can also
insert a start and stop command in your program to have a program
profiled every time it is run, or to profile only a part of the program:

        : MYWORD        ( -- )
                        PROF_START      \ start profiling
                        ...             \ your program goes here
                        PROF_FINISH     \ stop profiling and write
                        ;               \ results to PROF.TXT

  A companion program for TCOM called PROF.SEQ is a standalone program to
profile TCOM programs, or any executable program into 16 byte buckets of
where executing insturctions spend most of their time.  PROF can be used
on F-PC programs, but will profile code words, rather than colon
defintions.

{

\ The count array: one cell per cell of list space, from PROF-LO for
\ PROF-SIZE bytes, at PROF_SEG (it was a 32k far segment).
VARIABLE PROF-LO
VARIABLE PROF-SIZE
VARIABLE PROF-BUF       0 PROF-BUF !
0 VALUE  PROF_SEG       \ the count array, 0 if none
1 VALUE  PROF-MIN       \ the smallest count reported
VARIABLE PSAVED         \ is the hook ours?

ALSO ASSEMBLER

CODE PROF-TICK  ( ip -- )       \ count a token, called by the trace hook
        R0 POP,                         \ the IP about to run
        R1 PROF-LO LI,    R1 R1 0 LD,
        R0 R0 R1 SUB,                   \ offset into list space
        R2 PROF-SIZE LI,  R2 R2 0 LD,
        R0 R2 1 BGEU,                   \ outside the array: skip
        R2 PROF-BUF LI,   R2 R2 0 LD,
        R0 R0 R2 ADD,
        R3 R0 0 LD,   R3 R3 1 ADDI,   R3 R0 0 ST,
   1 L: R1 TRUE LI,   R2 DBG-ON LI,   R1 R2 0 ST,     \ re-arm the hook
        NEXT,
        END-CODE

PREVIOUS

VARIABLE OLD-DEBUG      VARIABLE OLD-LO         VARIABLE OLD-HI

: SAVE&SET_VECS ( -- )          \ point the trace hook at PROF-TICK
                PSAVED @ PROF_SEG 0= OR ?EXIT
                'DEBUG @ OLD-DEBUG !  DBG-LO @ OLD-LO !  DBG-HI @ OLD-HI !
                ['] PROF-TICK 'DEBUG !
                PROF-LO @ DUP DBG-LO !  PROF-SIZE @ + DBG-HI !
                PSAVED ON  DBG-ON ON ;

: REST_VECS     ( -- )          \ give the trace hook back
                PSAVED @ 0= ?EXIT
                DBG-ON OFF
                OLD-DEBUG @ 'DEBUG !  OLD-LO @ DBG-LO !  OLD-HI @ DBG-HI !
                PSAVED OFF ;

: UNPROF_EXITFUNC ( -- )
                REST_VECS
                DEFERS BYEFUNC ;

' UNPROF_EXITFUNC IS BYEFUNC    \ link into bye function list

handle profhndl                 \ the profile save file handle
create crlf$ $0D c, $0A c,      \ a CRLF string

32 array prof_name

DEFER PROF-OUT  ( a n -- )      \ where report text goes

: >PROFFILE     ( a n -- )      profhndl hwrite drop ;

: prof.id       ( nfa -- )      \ the name, without its high bits
                prof_name 32 cmove
                prof_name c@ 31 and prof_name c!
                prof_name count bounds
                ?do     i c@ $7F and i c!
                loop    prof_name count prof-out ;

VARIABLE PROF-TOTAL

: PROF-TOTAL@   ( -- n )        \ add up every count
                0 PROF_SEG PROF-SIZE @ BOUNDS
                ?DO     I @ +
                CELL +LOOP DUP PROF-TOTAL ! ;

: PROF-CFA      ( ip -- cfa | 0 )       \ the word whose list holds ip
                DUP IP>CFA
                IF      DUP @ FIRST-DOES-CT U< 0=       \ a DOES> clause:
                        IF      DROP LIST>CFA EXIT      \ the defining word
                        THEN    NIP
                ELSE    2DROP 0
                THEN    ;

: (U.)R         ( n w -- a n )  \ n right justified in w columns
                >R 0 <# #S #> R> OVER - 0 MAX SPCS SWAP PROF-OUT PROF-OUT ;

: 1prof         ( count cfa -- )        \ one line of the report
                OVER PROF-MIN <
                IF      2DROP EXIT
                THEN
                crlf$ 2 prof-out
                OVER 10 (U.)R
                SWAP 100 UM* PROF-TOTAL @ 1 MAX UM/MOD NIP 5 (U.)R
                " %  " prof-out
                ?DUP
                IF      >name prof.id
                ELSE    " ?" prof-out
                THEN    ;

: (REPORT)      ( -- )          \ the counts, grouped by definition
                PROF_SEG 0= ?EXIT
                PROF-TOTAL@ DROP
                0 0                             ( count cfa )
                PROF_SEG PROF-SIZE @ BOUNDS
                ?DO     I @ ?DUP
                        IF      I PROF_SEG - PROF-LO @ + PROF-CFA
                                ( count cfa n cfa' ) DUP 3 PICK =
                                IF      DROP ROT + SWAP
                                ELSE    2SWAP 1prof
                                THEN
                        THEN
                CELL +LOOP  1prof
                crlf$ 2 prof-out  " Total: " prof-out
                PROF-TOTAL @ 0 (U.)R ;

: saveprof      ( -- )          \ write the profile results to PROF.TXT
                " PROF.TXT" profhndl ">handle
                profhndl hcreate abort" Failed to create profile save file"
                ['] >PROFFILE IS PROF-OUT
                (REPORT)
                crlf$ 2 prof-out                \ append a pair of CRLF's
                crlf$ 2 prof-out
                profhndl hclose drop ;

: .TYPE-CR      ( a n -- )      \ TYPE, with CR for a CRLF
                OVER crlf$ = IF 2DROP CR ELSE TYPE THEN ;

: .PROF         ( -- )          \ display the profile results
                ['] .TYPE-CR IS PROF-OUT
                (REPORT) CR ;

: prof_on       ( -- )          \ turn on profiling
                save&set_vecs ;

: prof_off      ( -- )          \ turn off profiling
                rest_vecs ;

: prof_start    ( -- )
                prof_off
                PROF_SEG ?DUP IF FREE DROP 0 =: PROF_SEG THEN
                LIMIT PROF-LO !                 \ list space so far
                XHERE ALIGNED LIMIT - PROF-SIZE !
                PROF-SIZE @ ALLOCATE ABORT" No memory for the profile"
                DUP =: PROF_SEG  PROF-BUF !
                PROF_SEG PROF-SIZE @ ERASE      \ fill array with zeros
                prof_on ;

: prof_finish   ( -- )
                prof_off
                saveprof ;

: prof          ( -- )
\+ unedit       UNEDIT
                prof_start
                interpret
                prof_finish ;
